# B8 — reject-parity eval_fail corpus (issue #221).
#
# `distinct` (a pipeline stage) and `scalar()` (a function) are NOT Loki
# v3.7.4 constructs — both are absent from its grammar and Loki rejects each
# with an HTTP 400. Parity therefore means PulsusDB rejects them too; these
# `eval_fail` cases pin that rejection (the `msg:` substring is a stable
# fragment of PulsusDB's parse-error Display). The reference-rejects side is
# additionally pinned by the reject-parity registry disposition + the live
# differential leg (see the conformance harness).
#
# provenance: derived
# (file default; see logqltest/PROVENANCE.md §provenance markers.
#  A row may override it with its own `# provenance:` line.)

load
  {env="prod", service_name="rp"}
  0s  x=1

# `| distinct` falls through to the label-filter parser (no such stage in the
# grammar), which fails on the missing operator — a generic syntax error,
# never a misleading `NotYetSupported` placeholder.
eval_fail instant at 60s {service_name="rp"} | distinct foo
  msg: label-filter operator

# `scalar()` is not a recognized aggregation function — a generic rejection.
eval_fail instant at 60s scalar(rate({service_name="rp"}[1m]))
  msg: aggregation function
